/16/ringo-starr-all-starr-band-live-festival-hall-melbourne/\">Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Festival Hall, Melbourne</a></li><li>1999: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1999/02/16/ringo-starr-all-starr-band-live-beacon-theatre-new-york-city/\">Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Beacon Theatre, New York City</a></li><li>1979: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1979/02/16/mixing-reception-wings/\">Mixing: Reception by Wings</a></li><li>1977: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1977/02/16/photography-john-lennon-yoko-ono-stockbridge-usa/\">Photography: John Lennon and Yoko Ono in Stockbridge, USA</a></li><li>1977: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1977/02/16/recording-london-town-wings/\">Recording: London Town by Wings</a></li><li>1976: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1976/02/16/recording-cook-of-the-house-wings-2/\">Recording: Cook Of The House by Wings</a></li><li>1973: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1973/02/16/sequencing-red-rose-speedway-wings-2/\">Sequencing: Red Rose Speedway by Wings</a></li><li>1973: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1973/02/16/beatles-file-lawsuit-to-stop-alpha-omega-compilation/\">The Beatles file lawsuit to stop Alpha Omega compilation</a></li><li>1972: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1972/02/16/wings-live-town-hall-leeds/\">Wings live: Town Hall, Leeds</a></li><li>1972: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1972/02/16/recording-woman-is-the-n-r-of-the-world-john-lennon-yoko-ono/\">Recording: Woman Is The N****r Of The World by John Lennon and Yoko Ono</a></li><li>1971: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1971/02/16/recording-i-dont-want-to-be-a-soldier-well-baby-please-dont-go-john-lennon/\">Recording:  I Don’t Want To Be A Soldier, Well (Baby Please Don’t Go) by John Lennon</a></li><li>1970: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1970/02/16/tape-copying-mccartney-paul-mccartney/\">Tape copying: McCartney by Paul McCartney</a></li><li>1968: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1968/02/16/john-lennon-and-george-harrison-arrive-in-rishikesh/\">John Lennon and George Harrison arrive in Rishikesh</a></li><li>1967: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1967/02/16/recording-mixing-good-morning-good-morning/\">Recording, mixing: Good Morning Good Morning</a></li><li>1965: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1965/02/16/recording-i-need-you-another-girl-yes-it-is/\">Recording: I Need You, Another Girl, Yes It Is</a></li><li>1964: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1964/02/16/beatles-ed-sullivan-show/\">The Beatles’ second Ed Sullivan Show</a></li><li>1963: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1963/02/16/live-carfax-assembly-rooms-oxford/\">The Beatles live: Carfax Assembly Rooms, Oxford</a></li><li>1962: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1962/02/16/live-tower-ballroom-new-brighton-wallasey-11/\">The Beatles live: Tower Ballroom, New Brighton, Wallasey</a></li><li>1962: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1962/02/16/live-technical-college-hall-birkenhead-2/\">The Beatles live: Technical College Hall, Birkenhead</a></li><li>1961: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1961/02/16/live-litherland-town-hall-liverpool-6/\">The Beatles live: Litherland Town Hall, Liverpool</a></li><li>1961: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1961/02/16/live-cassanova-club-liverpool-3/\">The Beatles live: Cassanova Club, Liverpool</a></li></ul><p>Want more? Visit the <a title=\"Day after day: the Beatles' history\" href=\"/history/\">Beatles history section</a>.</p></div><div class=\"gm-map\" style=\"position: relative;height: 390px; width: 100%;\"><iframe data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"about:blank\" name=\"gm-map-1\" allowfullscreen=\"\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/?geo_mashup_content=render-map&amp;map_data_key=bc8490f6b40a09f28011ac4a568432fa&amp;height=390&amp;width=100%&amp;add_overview_control=false&amp;zoom=16&amp;enable_street_view=false&amp;map_type=G_HYBRID_MAP&amp;name=gm-map-1&amp;object_id=119638&amp;map_content=single\" style=\"position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: none; overflow: hidden;\" title=\"Geo Mashup Map\"></iframe></div>",
  "textContent": "The Beatles were photographed for the cover of their debut album Please Please Me on 16 February 1963. It was McBean’s second shoot with the band. An attempt earlier in the month was deemed unsuccessful, although an image from the session was used on the UK EP The Beatles’ Hits and on the US album Introducing The Beatles.\n\nThe final shoot took place at EMI House in Manchester Square, London. The photographer was Angus McBean.As I went into the door [of EMI House] I was in the staircase well. Someone looked over the banister – I asked if the boys were in the building, and the answer was yes. ‘Well,’ I said, ‘get them to look over, and I will take them from here.’I only had my ordinary portrait lens, so to get the picture, I had to lie flat on my back in the entrance. I took some shots and I said, ‘That’ll do.’Angus McBeanMcBean took a number of images of The Beatles looking over the balcony. In addition to the one used on Please Please Me, outtakes were used on the cover of the UK EP The Beatles (No.1) and the Red and Blue compilations The Beatles 1962-1966 and The Beatles 1967-1970.The outtakes from the session were lost in 2003 by Apple Corps.\n\n\n\n\n\nThe Beatles recreated the Please Please Me shoot in 1969 for the aborted Get Back album. An image from that session was also used on the Red and Blue albums. The Get Back album was released in October 2021 as part of the Let It Be super deluxe CD and vinyl box sets.\n\n\nPage last updated: 21 February 2024Also on this day...2025: TV: Paul McCartney on Saturday Night Live2013: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Festival Hall, Melbourne1999: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Beacon Theatre, New York City1979: Mixing: Reception by Wings1977: Photography: John Lennon and Yoko Ono in Stockbridge, USA1977: Recording: London Town by Wings1976: Recording: Cook Of The House by Wings1973: Sequencing: Red Rose Speedway by Wings1973: The Beatles file lawsuit to stop Alpha Omega compilation1972: Wings live: Town Hall, Leeds1972: Recording: Woman Is The N****r Of The World by John Lennon and Yoko Ono1971: Recording:  I Don’t Want To Be A Soldier, Well (Baby Please Don’t Go) by John Lennon1970: Tape copying: McCartney by Paul McCartney1968: John Lennon and George Harrison arrive in Rishikesh1967: Recording, mixing: Good Morning Good Morning1965: Recording: I Need You, Another Girl, Yes It Is1964: The Beatles’ second Ed Sullivan Show1963: The Beatles live: Carfax Assembly Rooms, Oxford1962: The Beatles live: Tower Ballroom, New Brighton, Wallasey1962: The Beatles live: Technical College Hall, Birkenhead1961: The Beatles live: Litherland Town Hall, Liverpool1961: The Beatles live: Cassanova Club, LiverpoolWant more? Visit the Beatles history section.",
